the result needs both components, a binary einsum: einsum spec "p^q; 2*p => p, q": one tensor's axes need both p and q, components of the concatenated axis p^q, but a position of that axis lies in one segment, so no position has both and the operation would compute nothing. Name one component per tensor (x ++ "a^b => a" takes a segment; (x, y) ++^ "a; b => a^b" joins two)
