an operand needs both, another fills one: the refusal says why: true
a shared first segment, a^b, a^c => a: einsum spec "a^b, a^c => a": the component a names segments of two different concatenated axes of one tensor, a^b and a^c, so only the blocks where both axes are in segment a would be reached (their diagonal), and the two concatenations would become one set of alternatives. On one tensor, a component may repeat only with its whole concatenation (a^b, a^b => a^b is its diagonal, like aa => a). For the diagonal of two segments, extract them under distinct labels first: x ++ "a^b, d^c => a, d", then ++ "aa => a"
a shared first segment, a^b, a^c => a: the refusal says why: true
