integers alone, a closed operand: einsum spec "a => 2^3": no operand names a component of the concatenated result axis 2^3, so nothing says what its segments hold. To write part of the axis, name the segment (a => 2^a^3 writes a between two skipped segments); to repeat a reduced operand in every cell, use a plain axis and size it (x ++ "a => b" ["b"], then Shape.set_dim b 5)
