the result needs the segment only the other operand has: Concatenation in einsum spec "a; b => a^b, b" of n2: no segment of a concatenated axis reaches operand(s) 1 (counted from 1). A position of that axis lies in one segment, and the result and each operand can only use the segment it lies in: the result or the operand needs another one, or two at once, so the operand would never be read
the result needs the segment only the other operand has: the refusal says why: true
